---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="About" section="about">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">About</p>
      <h1>Notes for people who build robots.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the learning side of Everything Robotics: a growing set of articles that explain one piece of a
        robot at a time, in the order you would need them to understand a real machine.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose" style="max-width: var(--measure)">
      <h2>How the articles are written</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Reasoning first.</strong> Each article explains why a design exists and what it trades away, before any catalogue of parts.</li>
        <li><strong>Sourced.</strong> Claims about a specific product, company or paper link to where they came from. Vendor-reported numbers are labelled as vendor-reported.</li>
        <li><strong>Dated.</strong> Robotics hardware moves quickly. Every article shows when it was last updated, and "recent" always means "as of that date".</li>
        <li><strong>Typical, not exact.</strong> Ranges such as gear ratios and efficiencies are typical engineering values. Check a datasheet before designing around them.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Topics</h2>
      <p>
        Articles are grouped into topics — actuators, dynamics, sensors, control, perception, learning and more.
        A topic page lists what is published and what is planned, so an empty topic is visibly empty rather than
        padded.
      </p>
      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If something is wrong or out of date, open an issue on the
        <a href="https://github.com/TechBOiz/robotics-learn">GitHub repository</a> with the source that
        shows the correct information.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
